    "result_text": "The build is green. The change is complete and fully verified.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `membershipNumber` field formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (YY = last two digits of the registration year, e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`), following the OfficeFloor function-injection pattern used for the sibling `customerCode` feature.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `membershipNumber` field mapped to `@Column(name = \"membership_number\")` with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`AssignOwnerMembershipNumber.java`** (new) \u2014 an OfficeFloor step that reads the `@Val Owner`, computes `registrationDate.getYear() % 100`, and sets `membershipNumber` = `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, yy)`.\n\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `assignMembership` step into the pipeline right after `assignCode` (so `customerCode` is set) and after `build` (so `registrationDate` is set), under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name onto both POST and GET responses.\n\n5. **DB schema** \u2014 added a `membership_number` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres), and appended the corresponding `NULL` to the positional seed inserts in the hsqldb `data.sql` (the other DBs use column-list inserts, so they were unaffected).\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` test and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
